🧠 Product Category × Demographics Analysis (Heatmap)

🎯 Objective
Analyze how product category sales vary across customer age groups to identify demographic-driven purchasing patterns and high-value customer segments.

🔧 Methodology
A pivot table was created to aggregate total sales by product department and customer age group. This matrix was used to generate a heatmap for visual comparison of spending intensity across segments.
merged.pivot_table(
    index=["DEPARTMENT"],
    columns=["AGE_DESC"],
    values="SALES_VALUE",
    aggfunc="sum",
    observed=False
)

📊 Insight
The analysis indicates that core retail categories such as GROCERY, DELI, DRUG GM, PRODUCE, and KIOSK-GAS consistently generate the highest sales across all age groups.
Spending intensity is highest among 35–54 year-old customers, suggesting that this segment represents the primary revenue driver. 
In contrast, younger customers (19–24) show more selective purchasing behavior, while older segments (55+) exhibit lower but more stable consumption patterns focused on essential goods.

💼 Business Value
This analysis supports:
Category-level demand understanding
Age-based customer segmentation
Targeted marketing strategies
Product assortment optimization
Customer value identification
